Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||08:22 PM||||Just curious... I've never seen a remote Fuel Pressure gauge- only the ones mounted right on the engine.  Does a remote one install the same way? Does it just send a signal to the guage via a pair of wires...or how?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Nashco||11-05-2001||11:40 PM||||I don't think I've ever seen an electric fuel pressure guage.  I had always assumed you could just use an oil pressure guage for this.  You'd have to mock up your own sending unit adapter for an oil pressure switch to screw onto the schrader valve, but it should work the same.  I plan on putting a fuel PSI guage on my other car as I explained, so I can monitor the system.<P>I plan on first seeing if the guage will retain normal operation if you run the wires through a switch.  I would like to be able to switch sender units between oil psi and fuel psi, so that I would only need one guage.  I doubt I'll ever have to monitor low oil pressure and low fuel pressure at the same time, and if I do, watching the guage is the least of my worries  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I like the pod guages...someday when I can afford it, and after the back-lit guage faces are available, I'll do it.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>*edited for type...had a lot lately! URG<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
